    <value>At each meal (3 times daily)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_TwentyMinute_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Take at least 20 minutes to eat</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_TwentyMinute_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Allows satiety signals to register, preventing overeating.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_FrontLoad" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Front-Load Calories</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_FrontLoad_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bigger breakfast</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_FrontLoad_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Eat bigger breakfast, smaller dinner</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_FrontLoad_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Aligns eating with circadian rhythm for better metabolism.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_TimeRestricted" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Time-Restricted Eating</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_TimeRestricted_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Under 12 hours, ending before 7 PM</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_TimeRestricted_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Eat within a daily window of under 12 hours that you can keep up every day of the week. It should end before 7:00 PM.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_TimeRestricted_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>May improve metabolic health and weight management.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Deflour" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Deflour Your Diet</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Deflour_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Intact grains instead of flour</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Deflour_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose intact grains over flour products</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Deflour_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Intact grains have lower glycemic impact and better satiety.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_BlackCumin" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Black Cumin</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_BlackCumin_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1/4 tsp daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_BlackCumin_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Also known as Nigella sativa. It is different from regular cumin, which has a different dose.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_BlackCumin_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>May help with weight loss and blood sugar control.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Garlic" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Garlic Powder</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Garlic_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1/4 tsp daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Garlic_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Add garlic powder to your food every day.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Garlic_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Studies show it can reduce body fat.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Ginger" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ground Ginger or Cayenne</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Ginger_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1 tsp ginger or 1/2 tsp cayenne daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Ginger_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stir ground ginger into hot water or chai; it may work better in the morning than in the evening. Or add 1/2 tsp of red pepper powder or 1 raw jalapeno to your day.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Ginger_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In randomized trials, ground ginger significantly decreased body weight. Red pepper may help activate calorie-burning brown fat.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NutritionalYeast" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nutritional Yeast</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NutritionalYeast_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2 tsp daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NutritionalYeast_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Beta-glucan fiber source</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NutritionalYeast_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Beta-glucan fiber can facilitate weight loss.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Cumin" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cumin</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Cumin_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1/2 tsp with lunch and dinner</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Cumin_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Regular cumin spice</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Cumin_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>May help with weight loss and improve cholesterol.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_GreenTea" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Green Tea</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_GreenTea_Desc_Imperial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3 cups daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_GreenTea_Desc_Metric" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>720 ml daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_GreenTea_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Drink it between meals, waiting at least an hour after eating so it doesn't interfere with iron absorption. Avoid large amounts of caffeine within 6 hours of bedtime.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_GreenTea_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Contains catechins that may boost metabolism.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Hydrated" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stay Hydrated</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Hydrated_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Urine no darker than pale yellow</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Hydrated_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check this off if your urine never looks darker than pale yellow. Riboflavin-fortified foods like nutritional yeast can color your urine, so if you eat them, aim instead for 9 cups (about 2 liters) of unsweetened drinks a day for women or 13 cups (about 3 liters) for men.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Hydrated_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Proper hydration supports metabolism and reduces hunger.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_ExerciseTiming" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exercise Timing</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_ExerciseTiming_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fasted, usually before breakfast</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_ExerciseTiming_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Any time is good, but there may be an advantage to exercising in a fasted state, at least 6 hours after your last meal. Typically that means before breakfast.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_ExerciseTiming_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>May enhance fat burning and metabolic benefits.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Sleep" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Get Enough Sleep</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Sleep_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>7+ hours</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Sleep_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Get at least 7 hours of sleep at your regular bedtime.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Sleep_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Poor sleep disrupts hunger hormones and metabolism.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_WeighTwice" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Weigh Yourself Twice</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_WeighTwice_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On waking and before bed</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_WeighTwice_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Weigh yourself twice a day, when you wake up and right before bed.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_WeighTwice_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Regular self-weighing is considered crucial for long-term weight control. The twice-a-day advice is based on one study.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Intentions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Implementation Intentions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Intentions_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Three if-then plans, each done daily</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Intentions_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Every two months, create three new "if X, then Y" plans for a specific behavior in a specific situation. Check off each one as you complete it every day.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Intentions_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Specific if-then plans help turn intentions into habits. In one randomized experiment, writing down when and where to floss more than doubled how often people did it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NightlyFast" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fast After 7:00 PM</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NightlyFast_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>12+ hours, starting before 7 PM</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NightlyFast_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fast every night for at least 12 hours, starting before 7:00 PM. The fewer calories after sundown, the better.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_NightlyFast_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Because of our circadian rhythms, food eaten at night is more fattening than the same food eaten earlier in the day.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Trendelenburg" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Mild Trendelenburg</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Trendelenburg_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sleep head-down 6 degrees</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Trendelenburg_LongDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Try spending at least 4 hours a night tilted head-down by 6 degrees, by raising the posts at the foot of your bed about 8 inches (20 cm).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Trendelenburg_Benefits" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A slight head-down tilt may boost fat burning, but the evidence is early. Use with caution.</value>
  </data>

