  </data>
  <data name="TT_Hydrated_Caution" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you have heart or kidney issues, talk to your doctor before drinking more.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_ExerciseTiming_Caution" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you have diabetes or prediabetes, start exercising 30 minutes after a meal begins instead, and ideally keep going for at least an hour.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TT_Trendelenburg_Caution" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Do not try this if you have heart or lung issues, acid reflux, or brain or eye problems. Even a family history of glaucoma rules it out. Ask your doctor first. Most people feel dizzy or faint if they stand up too fast afterward and could fall, so get up slowly. Drinking 2 cups (about 500 ml) of cold water 30 minutes before rising may help.</value>
